        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{-8x^6}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{-8x^6}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: root(\u2212 8x^{6}, 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}), 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2})^{3}, 3)|=; \u2212 2x^{2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: root(\u2212 8x^{6}, 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}), 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2})^{3}, 3)|=; \u2212 2x^{2}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{-8x^6}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n[MATH: root(\u2212 8x^{6}, 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}) \u22c5 (\u2212 2x^{2}), 3)|=; root((\u2212 2x^{2})^{3}, 3)|=; \u2212 2x^{2}]"
      },
